@startuml Routes Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox
title Routes — public lookup and internal ownership

actor Client
participant RouteController as Controller
participant "Get / Create / Update / Delete RouteService" as Service
database "MySQL\nRouteRepository" as Repository
participant "Owning content service" as Owner

alt Public lookup
  Client -> Controller : GET /routes or /routes/:id
  Controller -> Service : list or id
  Service -> Repository : find routes
  Repository --> Client : RouteResponseDto[] or route/null
else Content mutation
  Owner -> Service : create/upsert/delete route with entity identity
  Service -> Repository : choose unique path and persist with same transaction manager
  Repository --> Owner : RouteEntity or completion
end

note over Service, Repository
  Content services own when routes change.
  The repository prevents path collision and supports transactional writes.
end note
@enduml
